<title>UK: UK January gas production sets new record - WoodMac.</title>
<headline>UK January gas production sets new record - WoodMac.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average rate of natural gas produced in January in the U.K. set a new record at 12,327 million cubic feet a day (mmcfd), consultants Wood Mackenzie said in their March North Sea Report.</p>
<p>This is up by 256 mmcfd from the previous record of 12,074 mmcfd, set in February 1996. Output in January was also up by eight percent from the corresponding total in January 1996.</p>
